== Recent News

- \[November 2023\] We released our [https://github.com/NVlabs/mimicgen_environments MimicGen datasets and simulation environments]! The release includes over 48,000 task demonstrations across 12 tasks generated from just 120 human demos, and integrates directly with [https://robomimic.github.io/docs/datasets/mimicgen.html robomimic].

- \[November 2023\] 3 papers ([https://mimicgen.github.io/ MimicGen], [https://hitltamp.github.io/ HITL-TAMP], [https://mihdalal.github.io/optimus/ OPTIMUS]) presented at [https://www.corl2023.org/ CoRL 2023]. [https://mimicgen.github.io/ MimicGen] is an oral at the [https://generalist-robots.github.io/ CoRL 2023 Towards Generalist Robots Workshop] and [https://hitltamp.github.io/ HITL-TAMP] is an oral at the [https://corl2023deployable.github.io/ CoRL 2023 Deployable Workshop].

- \[May 2023\] We introduced [https://voyager.minedojo.org/ Voyager], the first LLM-powered embodied lifelong learning agent in Minecraft that continuously explores the world, acquires diverse skills, and makes novel discoveries without human intervention.

== About Me

I am a research scientist at NVIDIA AI working with [https://research.nvidia.com/person/dieter-fox Dieter Fox] in the [https://nvidia_srl.gitlab.io/ Seattle Robotics Lab]. I obtained my PhD degree from Stanford University, co-advised by [http://cvgl.stanford.edu/silvio/ Silvio Savarese] and [http://vision.stanford.edu/feifeili/ Fei-Fei Li]. My research focuses on developing systems and algorithms to enable robots to learn useful manipulation tasks.

